  <!-- ── Deeper Protocol ── -->
  <h2>The Deeper Protocol</h2>
  <ul class="insult-list">
    <li>No air filtration in the bedroom — unfiltered indoor air during your 7–8 hour recovery window</li>
    <li>HVAC filters changed less than quarterly — the system distributes whatever has accumulated</li>
    <li>Cooking without ventilation — gas stoves produce NO₂ and particulates that linger for hours</li>
    <li>Synthetic air fresheners and candles — a primary VOC source in many homes</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Fix sequence: bedroom HEPA unit first (protects your longest continuous exposure window) → HVAC filter on schedule →
    eliminate synthetic air fresheners and candles → mold test if brain fog and fatigue don't resolve.
    Source control matters as much as filtration.
  </p>

